        <idno type="URI">http://syriaca.org/work/5876</idno>
        <noteGrp type="abstract">
               <desc xml:lang="en">Abstract</desc>
               <note corresp="http://syriaca.org/nhsl" xml:lang="en" type="abstract" resp="http://syriaca.org">This collection of hymns from <persName ref="https://syriaca.org/person/51">Severus of Antioch</persName>/<persName ref="https://syriaca.org/person/113">Jacob of Edessa</persName> celebrates the <persName ref="https://syriaca.org/person/624">Virgin Mary</persName> for her role in the incarnation of Christ as God-bearer and her present role as a prayerful intermediary. These hymns colorfully allude to many events, personages, and imagery found within the Hebrew Bible, notably the creation story and God's covenant at Sinai.
               </note>
        </noteGrp>

